From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:48:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 160/162] GreatDANE: H1 StaticPrefs, H2 activation floor, M1/M3

H1: read greatdane.node.lazy and lazyTimeoutSec via StaticPrefs
(mirror: always) on the cert thread; drop the main-thread-only
Preferences::Get* calls. Defaults move out of firefox.js into
modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml (patch + fragment; this
overlay does not vendor the 20k-line file). The [1,60] clamp stays
in C++.

H2: restore the height >= activation floor in lazy mode. A test-only
pref/env (greatdane.node.lazyAllowPreActivation /
GREATDANE_LAZY_ALLOW_PRE_ACTIVATION, default off) allows pre-activation
fixtures. Fallback for a missing namespace_synced flag matches full
mode (floor + passes >= 1). Also require height+2 >= best_known_height
when that field is present and > 0.

M1: a cert/NSS failure is never relabelled as GD_ZONE_LOADING.
M3: lazy sync rules follow the mode the node was spawned with
(c.lazy / status.lazy), not the live pref.

M2, M4, and M5 are deferred (no mach).
